ts(frame, colors: Optional[Iterable[int]] = None, min_area: int = 1) -> List[Blob]:`; calls: Blob, arr, int, len, max, min, range, sorted, sum\n- L82--89 `def block_signatures(frame, cell: int = 4) -> Dict[Tuple[int, int], Tuple[int, ...]]:` — Partition a frame into fixed cells and return each cell's color signature.; calls: arr, int, range, sorted, tuple\n- L92--110 `def object_candidates(frame, cell: int = 4, min_area: int = 4) -> List[dict]:` — A compact, game-agnostic object list from color components and cell signatures.; calls: arr, block_signatures, connected_components\n- L113--123 `def frame_delta(before, after) -> dict:`; calls: arr, int, len, zip\n- L126--133 `def action_deltas(env, actions: Sequence[int] = ACTIONS) -> Dict[int, dict]:`; calls: arr, frame_delta, int\n- L136--142 `def replay(env, actions: Sequence[int]):`; calls: int\n- L145--153 `def path_result(env, actions: Sequence[int]) -> dict:`; calls: bool, color_counts, int, len, object_candidates, replay\n- L156--161 `def changed_signature(env, actions: Sequence[int], cell: int = 4):`; calls: block_signatures, replay, set, sorted\n- L164--186 `def bounded_bfs(env, goal_fn, actions: Sequence[int] = (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT, USE), key_fn=None, max_states: int = 20000, max_depth: int = 80):` — Generic clone BFS over observational keys. Use small max_states first.; calls: arr, deque, goal_fn, int, key_fn, len\n- L189--229 `def bounded_replay_bfs(env, goal_fn, action_fn, key_fn=None, max_states: int = 20000, max_depth: int = 80):` — Path-only BFS for games whose deep Arena clones become expensive.; calls: action_fn, arr, deque, goal_fn, int, isinstance, key_fn, len, reconstruct\n- L232--233 `def level_goal(base_level: int):`\n\n## solve.py\n- L3--13 `def solve(env): # dispatch to the per-level player for the current level, in a loop`; calls: fn, getattr\n# Unverified frontier brief: bp35 level 7\n\nThis is a compact index of the latest clean WIP, not solver evidence.\nReproduce every observation you rely on with the documented local API.\nDo not reread the full proposer transcript unless a named ambiguity requires it.\n\n## Verified parent budget\n\n- Exact parent boundary: level 6 at 196 actions.\n- Remaining real-action budget under the harness cap: 404 of 600.\n- This budget is verifier evidence. If it is insufficient, optimize earlier composed legs rather than searching an uncommittable suffix.\n\n## Prior proposer progress\n\n- At step 41, unsafe/convergent paths collapse to 62 distinct final roots. The probe is now trying the exact claimed suffix form on each: one visible setup action, four left moves, then the lowest visible gravity switch.\n- The expanded probe’s code omits the one candidate explicitly suggested by the scaffold wording: an inert coordinate click. It tests supports, controls, movement, and undo, but not a no-op click. The baseline no-op failed, yet the other 61 decoded roots have not been freshly tested with it. I’m stopping the broad 19–25-action-per-root loop and testing exactly that missing no-op suffix across all decoded roots.\n- The no-op-only probe has reproduced the same 96 step-23 states. It is traversing to the 62 final roots; unlike the previous broad loop, each root will now require only six actions, so the suffix phase should fit comfortably.\n- The deterministic 96-state middle is still the dominant cost; no reward transition has occurred. Once step 41 prints, the remaining no-op checks are small.\n- The no-op suffix has now been falsified on roots 0–28. Several roots expose the distinctive `(27,62)` and `(33,62)` switch pairs mentioned in the prior brief, but none increases reward after no-op + four left + lowest switch.\n- The no-op hypothesis is now fully falsified across all 62 decoded roots. The preserved 60-action scaffold is not recoverable by a single final setup action. I’m moving to a fresh local search from the strongest reproduced final root, using the actual observed controls/supports and reward rather than the scaffold’s fixed suffix.\n- The fresh local BFS starts after the baseline final switch at avatar cell `(4,0)`. No target or gravity control is visible, but seven supports remain; the search is testing movement, undo, and nearby support changes to depth 14 with the real reward as the only acceptance criterion.\n- The post-switch BFS has expanded 203 action successors and found 121 distinct public/selected-support states. None changes reward or reveals a target/control yet.\n- At 405 successors the search has 208 distinct states and still no reward, target, or control. It is completing the planned 500-expansion bound; this branch is looking like a closed post-switch chamber.\n- The bounded post-switch chamber produced 246 states without reward, so I’m closing that suffix for now. I found another concrete omission in the 62-root setup probe: it never tests color-15 hazards, even though earlier levels require interacting with them and several are visible in the final rooms. I’m testing exactly one hazard setup + four left + lowest switch across all decoded roots.\n- The hazard-only decode again reaches 96 states at step 23 with no reward. It is traversing to the 62 final roots; each root has only a handful of hazard clicks, so the suffix phase remains bounded.\n- The 96-state deterministic middle is still running; no branch has changed reward. This is the same reproducible cost profile as the no-op scan, not a new state explosion.\n\n## Preserved local probes\n\n- `frontier_scaffold.json` (2713 bytes)\n- `probe_l7.py` (3702 bytes)\n- `probe_l7_bridge71.py` (5384 bytes)\n- `probe_l7_cleanroom.py` (1627 bytes)\n- `probe_l7_combos.py` (2270 bytes)\n- `probe_l7_control_insertions.py` (2362 bytes)\n- `probe_l7_corrected_gap.py` (2177 bytes)\n- `probe_l7_corridor_effects.py` (1596 bytes)\n- `probe_l7_coupled_decode.py` (9164 bytes)\n- `probe_l7_decode_matrix.py` (5247 bytes)\n- `probe_l7_decode_roots.py` (2338 bytes)\n- `probe_l7_decoded_trace.py` (1873 bytes)\n- `probe_l7_dire